odl_tb5: RX copy that cannot drop a message, no stale DMA tunnel after unload

Applies on top of 0001 and 0002 (git apply, from the OdinLink-Five root).

1. RX MSG_END fallback copy (driver/odl_tb5_ring_dma.c). When the spare
   assembly buffers (rx_asm_pool) run dry -- routine while RCCL moves big
   buffers and the reader falls behind -- MSG_END copied the message with
   kmalloc(len, GFP_ATOMIC): an order-8 request for a 1 MiB message that
   cannot reclaim or compact. On a fragmented host it failed, the message was
   discarded, and both RCCL ranks hung in the collective until restart. The
   RX callback runs from the thunderbolt core's ring_work (the ring has no
   start_poll), so it may sleep: the copy is now kvmalloc(GFP_KERNEL)
   (reclaim, compaction, vmalloc fallback), freed with kvfree, and E2E flow
   control holds the sender meanwhile. might_sleep() documents the context.

2. Module exit (driver/odl_tb5_service.c). Devices attached with bind_any
   have no tb_service, so they were freed by an orphan loop that skipped
   disabling the XDomain paths, releasing the HopIDs, dropping the xdomain
   reference and removing the devm detach action. The DMA tunnel stayed in
   the thunderbolt core (the next load failed enable_paths with -ENOMEM until
   a reboot or cable replug) and the devm action would have called into the
   unloaded module when the XDomain went away. They now go through
   odl_tb5_destroy() after the action is removed.

3. Path enable (driver/odl_tb5_transport_nhi.c). Before enabling, tear down
   any DMA tunnel routed to the two NHI rings the instance holds: rings are
   exclusive, so such a tunnel is stale (left by an older build's unload).
   HopIDs are wildcards, rings are not, so ThunderboltIP's tunnel to the same
   XDomain is never touched. This recovers a link that item 2 would have
   prevented, without a reboot.

Validated on the two-box rig: rx_asm_pool=0 (every message through the new
copy) and the default pool, 1-64 MiB RCCL all-reduces with exact results,
with and without CPU load on both boxes; the stale tunnel on Box1 cleared at
load; full model serving afterwards.

